# Keeps the build context small and keeps things that must never reach a layer out of one.
#
# Note that both Dockerfiles COPY explicit paths rather than the whole tree, so nothing here
# is load-bearing for correctness of the agent image - it is for context size, and for the
# guarantee that a secret cannot be picked up by a future wildcard COPY.

**/bin/
**/obj/
TestResults/

# MinVer reads git history for the version, but the version is passed in as a build arg
# precisely so the image never needs .git.
.git/
.github/

# Never. backup/old-grafana/grafana.db is another system's credential database.
backup/
secrets/

tests/
docs/
charts/
*.md

# Dev-time only: the Tiltfile and the watch image it builds have no place in a release layer.
Tiltfile
Dockerfile.dev

# Manifests are applied to a cluster, not built into an image.
infra/

# ...except this one. infra/chaos/faulty-service/Dockerfile builds the C10 fixture with the
# REPO ROOT as its context - it has to, because the project inherits Central Package
# Management from /Directory.Packages.props and its TFM from /Directory.Build.props, and a
# context that excludes those fails restore with NU1008. The blanket `infra/` rule above
# therefore broke that build: `COPY infra/chaos/faulty-service/...` cannot find a path the
# context excluded. Negations must come after the rule they carve out of.
!infra/chaos/faulty-service/
